{"nodes": [{"id": "planning_project_missed_lead_revenue_finder", "label": "Missed Lead Revenue Finder (project charter)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L1-L121", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "planning_project_core_value_priority", "label": "Core Value Priority", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L11-L16", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ordered deliberately: (1) show lost revenue in money terms is the hook that makes the product legible to a non-technical owner, (2) zero-effort capture is the moat and the v2 focus, (3) automatic recovery is the expansion. Value must be proven in dollars before asking for data access or autonomy."}, {"id": "planning_project_zero_effort_data_capture", "label": "Zero-effort data capture (the moat)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L14, L19-L20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Manual CSV upload puts the work on the customer, and roughly 90% of target customers will never gather or export lead data by hand. Automatic ingestion is therefore not a convenience feature but the defensible core of v2."}, {"id": "planning_project_leak_detection_engine", "label": "Leak detection rules engine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L36-L37", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lives in packages/core and was built TDD-first so the rules deciding what counts as a leaked lead are verifiable independently of any UI or data source."}, {"id": "planning_project_revenue_estimation_engine", "label": "Revenue estimation engine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L36-L37", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Converts detected leaks into a dollar figure \u2014 the single number the product sells \u2014 which is why dedupe correctness upstream is treated as a correctness-critical concern."}, {"id": "planning_project_milestone_v2_automated_lead_capture", "label": "Milestone v2.0 \u2014 Automated Lead Capture & Recovery", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L17-L31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces manual CSV upload with automatic ingestion plus proactive missed-revenue alerts, and accepts a backend and multi-tenant persistence as the cost of doing so."}, {"id": "planning_project_graduated_autonomy", "label": "Graduated autonomy posture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L83-L85", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decided 2026-08-23. v2 detects and notifies only; draft-and-approve follow-ups come next; full-auto unlocks later per approval-rate telemetry. Full autonomy on day one destroys trust on the first mistake, while approve-forever fails busy owners and defeats the product promise \u2014 so autonomy is earned from telemetry rather than granted."}, {"id": "planning_project_ingestion_order", "label": "Ingestion source order (webhooks and email first)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L78-L79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decided 2026-08-23: webhooks plus email forwarding first because they need zero platform approvals and work day one; CRM OAuth second; Gmail OAuth third; Meta last because App Review and Google verification add weeks of gated risk before any customer value."}, {"id": "planning_project_supabase_for_auth_and_db", "label": "Decision: Supabase for both auth and database", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L53-L56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen over Neon on 2026-08-24 despite the research doc recommending Neon. RLS policies need auth.uid(); with a single vendor the database reads the verified JWT natively, so tenant isolation genuinely lives in the DB rather than in application code. Neon's stateless HTTP driver additionally cannot hold the per-transaction setting the ingest role depends on."}, {"id": "planning_project_contact_split_into_email_and_phone", "label": "Decision: contact splits into email/phone in the DB", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L57-L61", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The in-memory Lead type keeps one polymorphic contact field and hydration sets contact = email ?? phone. A single unvalidated column cannot be deduped, and dedupe is what prevents the same person being counted twice \u2014 which would corrupt the one number the product sells."}, {"id": "planning_project_two_dedupe_mechanisms", "label": "Decision: two dedupe mechanisms, not one", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L62-L65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "lead_events.dedupe_key handles retried deliveries; lead_identities handles the same human arriving through different channels. One key cannot do both jobs, and a single lead may hold several contact points."}, {"id": "planning_project_ingest_role_without_bypassrls", "label": "Decision: ingest uses a NOBYPASSRLS role, not service_role", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L66-L70", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Webhook ingest has no auth.uid(), so the obvious move is the service key \u2014 which bypasses RLS entirely. Instead a dedicated ingest_role reads a transaction-local app.customer_id, so a handler bug cannot write across tenants. Verified under test; the service-role fallback was never needed."}, {"id": "planning_project_merge_policy_as_pure_function", "label": "Decision: merge policy is a pure function (mergeLeadFields)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L71-L73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keeping the merge rules as a pure function makes the logic deciding whether a second sighting of a lead improves or corrupts the record testable without a database."}, {"id": "planning_project_ingest_read_only_on_detection_settings", "label": "Decision: ingest is read-only on detection_settings", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L74-L77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An inbound webhook has no business changing a customer's configuration. Missing settings fall back to engine defaults instead of erroring, so detection is never blocked by absent config."}, {"id": "planning_project_backend_jump_accepted", "label": "Decision: backend jump accepted for v2", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L80-L82", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Multi-tenant DB plus serverless API is accepted into v2 scope because integrations cannot be hosted by a static PWA. All sources normalize into the same Lead schema feeding the existing core engine, so the jump adds infrastructure without forking the detection logic."}, {"id": "planning_project_deferred_scope", "label": "Explicitly deferred scope", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L29-L31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CRM OAuth connectors, Gmail read-only OAuth, the Meta stack (IG/FB/WhatsApp) and automated follow-up/booking are all deferred: the integrations because they require platform approvals that gate delivery, and the automation because autonomy is graduated and must be earned per the full-auto-booking seed."}, {"id": "planning_project_rls_grants_nothing", "label": "Lesson: RLS grants nothing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L90-L94", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Policies filter only within privileges a role already holds. Drizzle emits CREATE POLICY but never GRANT, so the first migration left the authenticated role unable to read anything (error 42501). Nothing warns you \u2014 the isolation test caught it. Fixed in migration 0002_grants.sql."}, {"id": "planning_project_negative_control_discipline", "label": "Lesson: a security test that cannot fail is worse than none", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L95-L97", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An isolation suite that passes unconditionally provides false assurance, so the negative control is run deliberately: loosen a policy and assert the suite goes red (npm run test:prove-isolation -w @missed-lead/db)."}, {"id": "planning_project_parser_silently_disabled_leak_rules", "label": "Lesson: the parser silently disabled three of four leak rules", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L98-L100", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "last_contact_at and next_follow_up_at were header-mapped but never written, so every CSV lead looked unanswered and only one rule effectively ran. Re-check this whenever the Lead shape changes."}, {"id": "planning_project_multi_tenant_postgres_on_supabase", "label": "Multi-tenant Postgres with RLS (packages/db)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L42-L49", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seven tables with RLS on all of them, isolation proven by test with a working negative control. Isolation is enforced in the database rather than the application so a handler bug cannot leak across tenants."}, {"id": "planning_project_normalized_lead_schema", "label": "Normalized Lead schema (single convergence point)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L80-L82", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every ingestion source normalizes into one Lead schema that feeds the existing core engine, so adding a source never forks leak detection or revenue estimation."}, {"id": "planning_project_csv_upload_as_backfill", "label": "CSV upload retained as backfill", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L82", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kept rather than removed so customers can load history and so the product still works before any integration is connected."}, {"id": "planning_project_packages_core", "label": "packages/core", "file_type": "code", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L7-L8, L36-L37", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "planning_project_packages_db", "label": "packages/db", "file_type": "code", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L44", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "planning_project_packages_ui", "label": "packages/ui (Tamagui design system)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One Tamagui component library shared by the Vite PWA and the Expo app so web and mobile do not diverge visually or in behavior."}, {"id": "planning_project_push_notifications", "label": "Continuous detection with push notifications", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Expo push on mobile plus PWA web push turn the product from something the owner must open into something that interrupts them with a dollar figure."}, {"id": "planning_project_non_technical_onboarding", "label": "Non-technical onboarding flows", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Onboarding is reduced to pasting a webhook URL or adding an email filter, because any step requiring developer skills reintroduces the friction zero-effort capture exists to remove."}, {"id": "planning_project_lead_identity_merge", "label": "Identity merge (lead_identities)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L45, L62-L65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "planning_project_webhook_idempotency", "label": "Webhook idempotency (lead_events.dedupe_key)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L45, L62-L65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "planning_project_local_jwks_token_verification", "label": "/api/health and /api/me with local JWKS (ES256) verification", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L47", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "planning_project_document_evolution_process", "label": "Phase/milestone document evolution process", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L102-L117", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PROJECT.md is revised only at phase transitions and milestone boundaries via /gsd-transition and /gsd-complete-milestone, so scope, validated capabilities and decisions are re-audited on a fixed cadence instead of drifting continuously."}], "edges": [{"source": "planning_project_missed_lead_revenue_finder", "target": "planning_project_core_value_priority", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L11-L16", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_missed_lead_revenue_finder", "target": "planning_project_milestone_v2_automated_lead_capture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L17-L31", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_missed_lead_revenue_finder", "target": "planning_notes_product_direction_auto_capture_decision_record", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L86", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_core_value_priority", "target": "planning_project_zero_effort_data_capture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L14", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_core_value_priority", "target": "planning_project_revenue_estimation_engine", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L13, L36-L37", "weight": 0.8}, {"source": "planning_project_zero_effort_data_capture", "target": "planning_project_milestone_v2_automated_lead_capture", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L14, L19-L20", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_milestone_v2_automated_lead_capture", "target": "planning_notes_product_direction_auto_capture_webhook_ingestion", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L24", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_milestone_v2_automated_lead_capture", "target": "planning_notes_product_direction_auto_capture_email_forwarding_ingestion", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L25", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_milestone_v2_automated_lead_capture", "target": "planning_project_push_notifications", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L26", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_milestone_v2_automated_lead_capture", "target": "planning_project_non_technical_onboarding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L27", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_milestone_v2_automated_lead_capture", "target": "planning_project_deferred_scope", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L29-L31", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_deferred_scope", "target": "planning_seeds_full_auto_booking_seed", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L30-L31", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_graduated_autonomy", "target": "planning_seeds_full_auto_booking_seed", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L85", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_graduated_autonomy", "target": "planning_project_deferred_scope", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L30-L31, L83-L85", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_ingestion_order", "target": "planning_notes_product_direction_auto_capture_integration_order", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L78-L79, L86", "weight": 0.8}, {"source": "planning_project_ingestion_order", "target": "planning_notes_product_direction_auto_capture_webhook_ingestion", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L78-L79", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_ingestion_order", "target": "planning_notes_product_direction_auto_capture_crm_oauth_connectors", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L79", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_ingestion_order", "target": "planning_notes_product_direction_auto_capture_gmail_oauth_read_only", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L79", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_ingestion_order", "target": "planning_notes_product_direction_auto_capture_meta_stack_integration", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L79", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_supabase_for_auth_and_db", "target": "planning_project_multi_tenant_postgres_on_supabase", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L53-L56", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_supabase_for_auth_and_db", "target": "planning_project_ingest_role_without_bypassrls", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L55-L56", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_ingest_role_without_bypassrls", "target": "planning_project_multi_tenant_postgres_on_supabase", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L66-L70", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_contact_split_into_email_and_phone", "target": "planning_project_two_dedupe_mechanisms", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L57-L65", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_contact_split_into_email_and_phone", "target": "planning_project_normalized_lead_schema", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L57-L60", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_two_dedupe_mechanisms", "target": "planning_project_webhook_idempotency", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L62-L65", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_two_dedupe_mechanisms", "target": "planning_project_lead_identity_merge", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/PROJECT.md", "source_location": "L62-L65", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_project_two_dedupe_mechanisms", "target": "planning_project_revenue_estimation_engine", "rela